An improved version, as I felt it would be beneficial.

• Makefiles have been verified and corrected.
BUILDING example:
make -f makefile.linux

Balance and Gameplay
• Reduced damage scaling per level:
• Sword damage is now calculated as: level * 0.75.
• Magic damage is now calculated as: level * 1.3.
• Retained multipliers for discovered swords: upgraded swords now effectively increase damage output.
• Verified shield and armor mechanics: each level provides an additional 5% damage reduction.
• Moved the optional, randomized absence of enemies to `config.ini`:
• `random_enemies: YES/NO` (disabled by default).
• Note: Bosses do not respawn after being defeated.
• The "Infinite Crystal" now also restores health based on the character's level.
• Reworked how multiple simultaneous spell hits are handled:
• Global temporary invulnerability no longer causes most hits to register as "miss!".
• Each spell now has its own internal damage-application interval.
• Ongoing (lingering) effects no longer deal all their damage instantaneously.

Bug Fixes
• Fixed an issue with the inventory pause: enemies no longer regenerate mana or progress their cooldowns while the game is paused.
• Removed the pause that occurred when obtaining an item from a chest; the notification now appears and disappears while the game continues to run.
• Fixed timer and control-related bugs that arose following the transition of game logic to frame-time-based calculations.
• Fixed a corruption issue with the `MAXFLOAT` macro, which previously allowed enemies to deal damage multiple times within a single attack.
• Fixed screen-darkening effects and final cutscenes for higher resolutions.
• Fixed issues where enemies could regenerate mana or cast spells during pauses. • The crystal effect is no longer canceled when transitioning to another map.
•Fixed `sdl_blitscale()`: transparency of the source surface is now preserved when using an increased resolution.
As a result, fade transitions work once again—not just at 320×240, but also when scaling is applied.
• Added fastfade parameter to `build/config.ini`:

Quality of Life (QoL) and Interface
• Added hotkeys, configurable via `config.ini`:
• 1 — Crystal;
• 2 — Ice;
• 3 — Steel;
• 4 — Wood;
• 5 — Rock.
• Key stats for sword, magic, and defense are now displayed in the inventory.
• Game settings are saved when exiting via the Options menu; a single, clear "Exit" option is provided.
• Added an image-scaling setting for fullscreen mode.
• A confirmation prompt now appears when attempting to overwrite an existing save slot from the main menu.
• The game prevents the use of healing potions when the character’s health is already full, thereby preserving the item.

Engine and Graphics
• Reworked the calculation of in-game time and movement speed relative to FPS.
• Fixed issues with animations, delays, and cooldowns that were previously dependent on frame duration.
• Added image scaling based on the selected resolution (native resolution / 2).
• Cleaned up `griffon.h`:
• Resolved the `MAXFLOAT` conflict.
• Updated function prototypes to use `(void)` for empty argument lists.
• Removed an implicit dependency on `SDL.h`.
• Modularized the codebase: separated into core game logic, configuration, save systems, debugging tools, and the editor.
• Simplified `config.c/.h`: parameters are now defined via a table, eliminating redundant code for loading and saving.

Debugging and Monster Control
Available when `showdbginfo` is enabled:

• F10 — Noclip (no-collision mode);
• F11 — God mode;
• F12 — Map selection and loading;
• F9 — Monster selection and toggling control between the player and a monster;
• F8 — Infight: monsters will attack one another. • F7 — map editor (see F1 within the editor).
As a precaution, make a backup of the `mapdb` folder.

